- [acc-beliefs-007] Teleological Progression of Complexity: naturalistic fallacy — The claim that growth towards complexity and intelligence is a 'universal law' risks conflating what is observed or 'natural' with what is inherently good or desirable, especially when applied to AI.
- [acc-beliefs-007] Teleological Progression of Complexity: unfalsifiability — The claim of a 'universal law' of growth towards complexity and intelligence is so broad and abstract that it is difficult to conceive of empirical evidence that could definitively disprove it.
